Origin: DHI
Description: Let the api.sh shutdown loop count under set -e.
 The graceful-shutdown handler waits for gunicorn with a while loop whose body
 increments a counter with ((count++)). Under `set -euo pipefail` that
 arithmetic command returns non-zero when the counter is 0, so bash exits the
 script about one second after SIGTERM with status 1 and gunicorn is not
 drained for SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT seconds. Use a plain assignment instead.
Forwarded: not-yet
Upstream: https://github.com/codecov/umbrella (tag self-hosted-26.7.6)
diff --git a/apps/codecov-api/api.sh b/apps/codecov-api/api.sh
index ba58d4ff1..da8783758 100755
--- a/apps/codecov-api/api.sh
+++ b/apps/codecov-api/api.sh
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ shutdown() {
     
     while kill -0 "$api_pid" 2>/dev/null && [[ $count -lt $timeout ]]; do
       sleep 1
-      ((count++))
+      count=$((count + 1))
     done
     
     # If process is still running, force kill
